rs + Enable-click flips to status='on') plus C3 best-effort (calibration panel renders when peer is connected — §B2 documented limitation) and M1–M8 manual-QA checklist. 33 new vitest tests (180 total, was 147 baseline): 18 motion (impulse threshold, exact debounce-boundary, 60s-rest, single + five-impulse + double-tap acceptance criteria, calibration p10 vs `min` at length 11, floor clamp, `getActiveThresholdG`), 5 motion-runner (armed/calibrating mode messages, setConfig reset, mode exposure), 8 wire (sample + config round-trips, NaN/Infinity/zero/negative threshold rejection, negative debounce rejection, unknown-mode rejection, missing-field rejection), 2 profiles (calibration round-trip, overwrite). Lint + tsc + vite build all clean. Bundle: main bundle UNCHANGED at 344.22 KB / 106.44 KB gzip (Phase 2b.2 baseline 344.20 / 106.45 — the +0 KB main-bundle preservation continues); PairScreen chunk 139.98 KB / 51.04 KB gzip (+3.09 KB raw / +0.87 KB gzip for CalibrateScreen, inside the lazy boundary); PhoneApp chunk 7.57 KB / 2.70 KB gzip (+3.16 KB raw / +1.03 KB gzip for motion + motion-runner, also inside its lazy boundary). Code-reviewer (`code-reviewer` agent) returned REQUEST-CHANGES with 2 blockers + 4 should-fix + 4 nits; blockers and the four cheap fixes (DRY accessor, `Date.now()`→`performance.now()`, debounce-boundary test, percentile test) plus three nits (NaN/Infinity guard on config, `MotionRunner.config` defensive copy, the debounce + percentile tests) were applied before approval. Findings deferred with rationale: #5 `finishCalibration` re-binds listener on profile update — currently harmless because status immediately transitions to 'done' after onSaved (reviewer agreed); #6 `peer.send` failure during `startCalibration` — the phone's default mode is 'armed', so a failed switch to 'calibrating' correctly leaves the phone in its prior armed state (the audit was wrong about the symmetry: there is no prior 'calibrating' state the phone could be stuck in). 